"It spends 1.0% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The company holds more cash than debt."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 3.4% over 3 years, 10.8% over 5 years and 3.7% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 17%).","At current returns, reinvesting 10% of profits supports about 2.6% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 3.4% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.3x, 1.4% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 15, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 4.4% on average."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 4.0%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 4 purchases and 1 sale over the past year, net $655K bought.","It returns 6.2% a year to shareholders (6.4% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 2.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 18.5% of the float, 8.4 days to cover."],"people":["With about 12,050 employees, each generates about $390K of revenue, in line with the Technology median, and productivity has risen 3.7% a year.","That works out to $20K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.3M (6x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":82,"head":"Invest: trades 81% below fair value of $131; ROIC 26.5% vs WACC 10.5%.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 47, gates 11/24)","Trades 81% below fair value of $131","ROIC 26.5% vs WACC 10.5%","Revenue grew 10.8%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA -0.4x"],"cons":["Interest coverage only 2.0x"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":111.04,"vc":{"base":130.63,"base_src":"dcf","bear":90.8,"bull":192.27,"alt_media